   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Our new name is going to be 'The Just Exactly Perfect Band'**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Sunrise**: back after 107 archived shows (469 days) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1979-12-29.137650.sen421.miller.sirmick.sbeok.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 24 songs; 166 min [1]. Said about its sound: Final thirty-one seconds of Terrapin Station contain no musical audio; Left channel of Johnny B. Goode is silent for first two and a half seconds [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer notes a date error in the posted recording file [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1979-12-29.137650.sen421.miller.sirmick.sbeok.flac16**: taped by Anon; transferred by Charlie Miller and SIRMick; source: Updated Source Info: Audience recording (Sennheiser 421s) > Cass x 2 > cdr > eac > wav 16/44.1; Recorded by Ron Ellner; Lineage: wav 16/44.1 > Adobe Audition… [1]. Also: Recording is a next-generation Maxell cassette transfer from source shnid 93234 [1]",
